152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (With the rapid growth of Artificial Intelligence and IoT, more applications are being deployed on edge devices such as smartphones, wearable devices, and sensors. During my research, I found that although Federated Learning provides a privacy-preserving way to train machine learning models, existing approaches perform poorly in real-world scenarios where devices have limited battery life, unstable internet connectivity, and varying computational capabilities.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (These challenges inspired me to work on an Energy-Aware Federated Learning framework that uses Deep Reinforcement Learning \(Deep Q-Network\) to intelligently select the most suitable clients for training. My goal is to improve energy efficiency, reduce communication costs, and enhance model performance in low-connectivity edge environments.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
